WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Hank, we had this big conversation about how you weren't gonna get me anything for my birthday,

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:10.060
because I didn't get you anything for your birthday, and then what should show up in our office but Nerd Fighters,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:15.760
the actual original video game! I'm a very happy person  right now. Thank you.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:21.360
I'd like to announce my retirement from writing and the fact that I am going to become a full ti- ahhh.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.000
I may not be ready to become a full-time nerd fighters player

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.080
because as soon as I announced my retirement... I lost.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.180
So Hank, good news and bad news. The bad news is that I'm now hundreds of miles away

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.180
from the AMAZING birthday present you got me, I- ahahahh!

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.700
The good news is that I'm back in Pittsburgh, on the set of the TFIOS movie.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.020
So, I always thought that when they made movies - by the way, this is Ben Richardson, the cinematographer

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.920
of the movie - I always thought when they made movies and there's like seven different angles in a shot,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:52.040
that it was seven different cameras, you know? But it turns out there''s just one very expensive camera

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:55.180
seven different times. [Ben:] Exactly. This was one of the great delights of my life,

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.800
was trying to explain this principle to my mom. The tricky thing is, if we had another camera right now,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.820
for the shots that we just got, the cameras would be right there, in front of the car -  [John:] Yeah! Of course.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:08.960
No, I realize that now, Ben! There's Deb. She does the [John tries to make snapping noise]. Action! [actual snapping noise]

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.940
One of the weird rules of making the movie is, we're not allowed to do anything until Deb hits the slate.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.520
Like, I can't eat until.. [Deb:] Marker. [Snap]

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.640
And if I wanna go to the bathroom... [Deb:] Marker. [Snap]

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.720
By the way, I was just, like, 'why do all these cars have Indiana license plates?'

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.560
And then I remembered, because of the movie!

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.140
So, Hank, I always thought that making movies was super glamorous, but it turns out that

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:32.820
it's mostly just a construction site. However, there is one very glamorous facet to the moviemaking process:

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.500
I am referring, of course, the the porta-potties.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.340
I mean, Hank, I've lived in apartments smaller than this porta-potty. It has both a toilet and a urinal.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.240
It also smells great in here, by the way. It smells like angles and stardust.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.000
I am serious. This is a FANCY porta-potty.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.620
Also, there's free food. Including... Atomic Fireballs, did you see that, Josh?

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:57.080
[Josh:] I did. Should we have Nat... cut. Should we have Nat maybe eat this right before he kisses Monica for the first time?

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:03.860
I'm here, with Isaac and Alex. "Hello," Isaac, "Hey," and Alex. And they were just saying that I should...

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:10.100
I should just stand in for Ansel. I am Gus. [Alex:] I mean, he looks, older than you, actually.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.980
[Isaac:] It's like the Olsen twins.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.780
But of course most of my time on set is spent watching and listening,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.780
although now with Nat Wolff making trouble in the background. Oh, Nat. I love you, too.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.520
So, Hank, one of my favorite things about the movie so far is they cast real teen cancer survivors

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.040
for the support group, they're waving to you right now, in fact.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.500
And I wanna thank all of them for being part of the movie, and also for sharing their experiences

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.040
with us, it's just been awesome to hang out with them. Mind if I send this to TMZ?

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.080
[Shailene:] Hello? Oh, hey, Sarah. What's up?

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:42.600
[John:] Can I tell you what's funniest about that? I turned the camera away when you answered the phone

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.260
because you're such a good actress that I thought you were really on the phone.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.740
[laughing] That's just pure talent.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:53.200
I'm here with Ansel Elgort, who's playing Gus in The Fault in Our Stars movie and has a blue tongue,

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.520
uhm, we're gonna do, like, a quick Question Tuesday and then people can submit questions

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.400
and then maybe we'll do another Question Tuesday in the future with real questions.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.340
But the question I get the most often is 'have you read the book?'. [Ansel:] Yeah, I've read it.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:11.060
[John:] Did you, what'd you think? [A:] It was alright. [J:] Yeah, yeah, it's a little- it was long in places.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:16.600
[A:] I loved it, I loved it. [J:] Um, and then, uhh... I think we're about to get hit by a car.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:22.260
Nightmare scenario! What's your last memory? Ansel Elgort's beautiful hand on my shoulder.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:27.440
Did you read the book? [Shai:] Yes. [J:] people ask me that all the time, though, like, they think you haven't

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.240
read the book. [S:] I read the book. I read the book multiple times. it's definitely one of my favorite books.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.240
[S:] meaning that it's kind of my second favorite- no, not my second favorite [J:]behind

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.180
[S:]It's in my, it's in my top two favorite books ever.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.060
[J:] Behind? [S:] I'd have to say that I really love "1984"

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.460
We gotta go apparently because somebody is about to make-out.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.440
It's not me. But, I'll see you on friday.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.720
[J:] Ansel, can you say see you on Friday? [A:] See you on Friday, Hank. [S:] Hasta luego amigo!

